<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“D- dog?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> <span style="color:Pink">replies in confusion, confirming your fear that he, in fact, does not see you as a dog but as his collared classmate without clothes,</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I- I don’t…”</span> He looks utterly bewildered. <span style="color:Pink">You try to explain what is happening, to the best you can, and maybe even ask him for help. But much to your horror, the only thing that comes out of your mouth is a bark. <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> just stares at you in utter shock, blushing as he tries not to look down at your exposed body. Your lip quivers as you realize how helpless you are.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“See, he’s excited.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“He loves going out like this, we did it all the time before we moved here, but we’ve been so busy I’ve been slacking my duty. But he loves it though.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“H- he does!?”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> looks at you, surprised by <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span>’s claim that you wanted this. <span style="color:Pink">You helplessly try to clear up the confusion, desperate for <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> not to think you are some pervert who likes to be walked naked by his brother, but once again the only thing that comes out are barks.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“R- right… I gotta go! I… yup…”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Lucas</span> <span style="color:BlueViolet">turns back to run inside but freezes as soon as he is no longer looking at you.</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:BlueViolet">He pauses, as if stunned, and you notice some sort of flickering around his eyes. Then he blinks and shakes his head.</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Huh, I didn’t know they had a dog. Cute.”</span> His voice sounds calm, almost normal. <span style="color:BlueViolet">As if he didn’t just see you collared and naked. He walks back inside and you notice him smiling idly… what is going on!?</span> <br>
<br>

<<linkreplace"Continue">>
    It takes you a few more humiliation encounters with strangers, classmates, and passersby to figure out what exactly is going on. <span style="color:Pink">Whenever someone, besides <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span>, is looking at you, they see you for what you really are. A boy on a leash forced to walk naked down the street by his brother. Their reactions vary, some look shocked, some confused, but most find it rather funny. Some high schoolers point and laugh, some kids make fun of you, an amused classmate even asks if he can pet you, which <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> allows. It is utterly humiliating.</span> <br>

