    The only bright side, if you can call it that, is what happens once they look away. <span style="color:BlueViolet">Once their eyes are off you, they seem to forget what exactly they saw and remember you as just a puppy. This means that, thankfully, no one will remember what happened,</span> <span style="color:Pink">but it still doesn’t make every teasing remark or hushed chuckle any less embarrassing.</span> <br>
    <br>
    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright, do your business so we can start heading home.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> says, stopping by a tree. <span style="color:LightCoral">You freeze. He doesn’t actually mean for you to…</span> <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Come on, hurry up.”</span> You try to refuse, pulling away to continue the walk to get it done as soon as possible, but <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Gabe</span> keeps you in place. <span style="color:BlueViolet">Then you feel it, a sudden urge to pee. The spirit inside of you seemingly making you do this…</span> <br>
    <br>
